<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#eventLocation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Location where the fieldwork event took place. Language-tagged string; may be general (city/country) for access-controlled records."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#contestedAuthorityOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#RitualAuthority> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#titleType-colonial-designation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The dc:title is a name or label assigned by colonial administrators, slaveholders, mission authorities, or overseers. Not the person or community's own name. This value should trigger elevated scrutiny of access governance and provenance documentation."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#Narrative> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A narrative cluster that may have multiple variants across place, time, authority, and lineage. First-class in Core so any domain module (Marca for odu essays, Ngoma for lyric traditions, Ékpè for origin stories) can attach narratives without importing the full narrative module."@en .
