<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#tradition-bantu-derived> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Traditions with primary roots in Bantu and Kongo religious culture. Bantu as a linguistic and cultural family spans Central, East, and Southern Africa; this concept primarily covers the Kongo-rooted Central African traditions most prominent in Afro-Atlantic contexts. For traditions specifically rooted in Southern or East African Bantu cultures, use or add appropriate region-specific concepts under iroko:region-central-african, iroko:region-east-african, or iroko:region-southern-african."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#SacredStatusScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#sacredStatus-hereditary-custody> .
