<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-core> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Cross-module infrastructure for governance and semantic integration of African and Afro-Atlantic sacred knowledge systems. Provides access control, provenance tracking, contested knowledge modeling, assertion governance, temporal variation, fieldwork capture, thin narrative primitives, archival person representation, and date precision modeling. Scope expanded to pan-African in v1.4.0."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#NarrativeVariant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A specific telling, transcript, or rendering of a narrative within a particular context, lineage, or temporal frame. The unit that carries text, language tag, authority scope, and access control."@en .
