<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#region-nile-valley> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Traditions with primary roots in the Middle Nile Valley, Upper Nile, Ethiopian highlands, and Eritrean plateau. Covers Christian Nubian civilization (Nobadia, Makuria, Alodia), Sudanic traditions, Ethiopian Orthodox and indigenous Ethiopian communities, and Ge'ez-language manuscript cultures. The geographic scope of materials in the Database of Medieval Nubian Texts (DBMNT, University of Warsaw) and the Hill Museum and Manuscript Library Northeast African collections."@en .
