<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ArchivalPerson> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A person documented in archival records within the framework. Distinct from foaf:Person and prov:Agent in being specifically a person-as-archived — defined by their documentary trace rather than by personal attributes. Intended for persons appearing in historical records, colonial documents, notarial instruments, plantation registers, ecclesiastical records, and similar materials across any geographic or temporal scope. A single iroko:ArchivalPerson instance may carry multiple documentary references pointing to the same individual across different archival sources. Subclass of iroko:Entity; not a subclass of iroko:SacredEntity, since archival persons are not necessarily tradition-specific sacred knowledge subjects."@en .
