<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#systemType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-core> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#variationContext> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#minimumAccessLevel> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#access-public-unrestricted> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#sacredStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#documents> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#minimumAccessLevel> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#access-public-unrestricted> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#sourceRelationship> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-core> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#assertionObject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The entity that is the object of the claim. Named assertionObject (not object) to avoid shadowing rdf:object. Range is intentionally untyped — the object of an assertion may be any resource inside or outside the framework, including external URIs, foaf:Person instances, geographic locations, or framework entities. Constraining the range would break the generality of the reification model."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#EpistemicTypeScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#epistemicType-political-reinterpretation> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#eventDate> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#minimumAccessLevel> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#access-public-unrestricted> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#tradition-lucumi> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#minimumAccessLevel> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#access-public-unrestricted> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#fieldworkProvenance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Details of fieldwork context if this knowledge derives from direct ethnographic observation."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#dateCentury> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The century in which an event occurred or a document was produced, expressed as an integer representing the century number (e.g., 13 for the thirteenth century, 6 for the sixth century). Use when only century-level precision is available — characteristic of medieval and ancient materials from corpora such as the Database of Medieval Nubian Texts and the Hill Museum and Manuscript Library. Pair with iroko:dateUncertain to flag where even the century assignment is provisional. Does not replace xsd:date — both may be asserted on the same instance when the exact date is also known."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#Narrative> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
