<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#TraditionScheme> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Controlled vocabulary of tradition classifications spanning continental African regional traditions and Afro-Atlantic derived traditions. Three tiers: (1) geographic region concepts (iroko:region-*) as the broadest level for continental African traditions; (2) cultural-linguistic family concepts (iroko:tradition-*-derived, iroko:tradition-calabari, iroko:tradition-kemetic) as mid-level groupings; (3) specific named traditions as leaves. Afro-Atlantic creole and syncretic traditions (iroko:tradition-haitian-vodou, iroko:tradition-syncretic, iroko:tradition-afro-indigenous, iroko:tradition-pan-african, iroko:tradition-new-orleans-voodoo, iroko:tradition-obeah) are top-level concepts not subordinated to the geographic hierarchy, because their origins are plural or their character is specifically New World or political. Expanded to pan-African scope in v1.4.0."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#consent-documented> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Documented Consent"@en .
