<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#tradition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The tradition to which this entity belongs. Values from iroko:TraditionScheme. May be a specific named tradition (e.g., iroko:tradition-lucumi, iroko:tradition-candomble-ketu, iroko:tradition-vodou-rada), a cultural-linguistic family (e.g., iroko:tradition-yoruba-derived, iroko:tradition-bantu-derived), or a geographic region (e.g., iroko:region-west-african, iroko:region-nile-valley). Scope is pan-African as of v1.4.0; not limited to Afro-Atlantic traditions."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#sacredStatus-replica-teaching> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Replica/Teaching Object"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#rejectingLineages> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#minimumAccessLevel> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#access-community-only> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#invocationText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Exact words, prayers, or songs recited when working with this entity — plant, spirit, or ceremony. Applies to any domain module. OPERATIONAL ONLY — never exported to public RDF."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#tradition-kromanti> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
