<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#TemporalVariation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named temporal regime, calendar cycle, or context that conditions how a property, assertion, or policy applies. Covers: ritual calendar seasons, festival-bound periods, pre/post-initiation thresholds, gender regime cycles, and any other time-bounded condition affecting sacred knowledge governance. TemporalVariation instances are named nodes shared across modules — define once, reference everywhere. Examples: iroko:TemporalVariation/egungun-festival-period, iroko:TemporalVariation/post-kariocha-year."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#tradition-fon-ewe-derived> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#region-west-african> .
